---
// SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only
// Hero: the promise beside a real Windows terminal. The specimen lines are what the CLI
// prints (src/TunnelTend/Public/90-Cli.ps1, human status and doctor renderers); nothing is
// a fictional dashboard. No Mac window chrome: this is a Windows tool.
import Icon from '../Icon.astro';
import CommandStrip from '../CommandStrip.astro';
import { INSTALL_COMMAND, LATEST_RELEASE, docPaths, paths } from '../../data/site';
---
<section class="hero">
  <div class="wrap hero-grid">
    <div class="hero-text">
      <p class="eyebrow">Unofficial Windows caretaker for OpenAI’s MCP tunnels</p>
      <h1 class="display for-plain">Keep the tools on your PC connected to ChatGPT.</h1>
      <h1 class="display for-dev">Your MCP servers, tunneled and tended.</h1>
      <p class="strap">Register once. Leave the routine to TunnelTend.</p>
      <p class="why for-plain">Have a tool with an MCP server—the program that lets ChatGPT use it? OpenAI’s official tunnel client makes the connection. TunnelTend handles the routine on your PC: starting registered services when you sign in, checking them, recovering within limits and keeping the official client updated. When something needs your attention, it says so.</p>
      <p class="why for-dev">OpenAI’s <code class="code-inline">tunnel-client</code> connects a local MCP server to Secure MCP Tunnels. TunnelTend wraps it in desired state: current-user Scheduled Tasks at sign-in, a watchdog with ownership checks and a visible retry budget, source watching, verified client updates with rollback, and read-only <code class="code-inline">status</code>, <code class="code-inline">health</code> and <code class="code-inline">doctor</code> with a stable JSON envelope.</p>
      <div class="hero-install">
        <p class="hero-fine">First time? <a class="link-quiet" href={`${docPaths.getStarted}#before-installation`}>Check your tool, PowerShell and OpenAI access</a> before installing.</p>
        <CommandStrip command={INSTALL_COMMAND} label="Copy the one-line install command" />
        <p class="hero-fine">Windows 11 · PowerShell 7.4+ · <a class="link-quiet" href={LATEST_RELEASE}>Latest release</a> · free and open source · <button class="reader-quiet" type="button" data-reader-toggle data-label-plain="Excuse me, I’m a dev?!" data-label-dev="I’m not a dev, actually" aria-pressed="false"><span data-reader-label>Excuse me, I’m a dev?!</span></button></p>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-ctas">
        <a class="btn btn-l btn-primary" href={paths.install}><Icon name="windows" size={15} />Install on Windows</a>
        <a class="btn btn-l btn-secondary" href="#how">How it works</a>
        <a class="hero-tertiary" href={docPaths.getStarted}>Read the full guide →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <figure class="win hero-win">
      <div class="win-bar"><span class="win-tab"><Icon name="terminal" size={13} />PowerShell</span><span class="spacer"></span><span class="win-glyphs" aria-hidden="true">—▢✕</span></div>
      <pre class="terminal" aria-label="A terminal showing tunneltend status and tunneltend doctor output"><span class="p">PS C:\Users\you&gt; </span><span class="c">tunneltend status</span>
<span class="ok">[OK]</span> internal-tools           desired=<span class="k">running</span> observed=<span class="ok">ready</span>     autostart=True watchdog=True
<span class="ok">[OK]</span> notes-search             desired=<span class="k">running</span> observed=<span class="ok">ready</span>     autostart=True watchdog=True
<span class="neu">[--]</span> photo-tagger             desired=<span class="k">stopped</span> observed=<span class="neu">stopped</span>   autostart=True watchdog=True

<span class="p">PS C:\Users\you&gt; </span><span class="c">tunneltend doctor</span>
No problems detected.

<span class="p">PS C:\Users\you&gt; </span><span class="c">tunneltend service stop photo-tagger --session-only</span>
<span class="dim">{'{"serviceId": "photo-tagger", "stopped": true}'}</span>
<span class="p">PS C:\Users\you&gt; </span><span class="cursor" aria-hidden="true">_</span></pre>
      <figcaption class="machine-foot">Example: three registered services, one stopped on purpose. Green means observed healthy locally. A session-only stop is respected by the watchdog until your next sign-in.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .hero { padding: 72px 0 56px; }
  .hero-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.9fr) minmax(0, 1.2fr); gap: 40px; align-items: center; }
  .hero-text { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 18px; }
  .display { font-size: 52px; line-height: 1.04; letter-spacing: var(--tracking-display); font-weight: 700; max-width: 14ch; }
  .strap { font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; margin: 0; color: var(--accent-text); }
  .why { margin: 0; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--fg-2); max-width: 52ch; }
  .hero-install { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; margin-top: 4px; }
  .hero-fine { margin: 0; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 12px; color: var(--fg-3); }
  .hero-ctas { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 10px; }
  .hero-tertiary { margin-left: 6px; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--fg-2); }
  .hero-tertiary:hover { color: var(--fg); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
  /* a real terminal wraps at its width; so does this one, instead of growing a scrollbar */
  .hero-win .terminal { font-size: 11.5px; white-space: pre-wrap; overflow: hidden; padding: 14px 14px; }
  .cursor { color: var(--machine-fg); animation: blink 1.1s steps(2, start) infinite; }
  @keyframes blink { to { visibility: hidden; } }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .cursor { animation: none; } }
  @media (max-width: 1100px) { .display { font-size: 44px; } }
  @media (max-width: 900px) { .hero-grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 28px; } .display { max-width: none; } }
  @media (max-width: 640px) { .hero { padding-top: 36px; } .display { font-size: 34px; } .strap { font-size: 18px; } .hero-win .terminal { font-size: 11.5px; } }
</style>
